    "narrative": "**Corbin Carroll** headline the slate as our premier offensive weapon, carrying an elite 82.37 efficiency score against Elder. With a favorable park factor and a top-two spot in the order, **Corbin Carroll** is our primary source for both counting stats and the stolen base upside we crave in this league. Alongside him, **Max Muncy** (68.95) and **Henry Bolte** (65.39) benefit immensely from a highly exploitable matchup against Bradford. The significant SP skill gap (+19% boost) and favorable wind/park conditions elevate both into high-conviction plays, with **Henry Bolte**\u2019s leadoff designation providing extra leverage for potential runs. **Mickey Moniak** also projects well at 66.31, bolstered by a dynamic platoon advantage and wind blowing out, making him a sneaky high-ceiling start despite a lower base projection.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Jose Caballero**, who missed the cut with a 39.32 score, falling just shy of our 40-point \"zebra\" threshold. While **Jose Caballero** remains a roster staple for his elite speed, the combination of a daunting matchup against Cease and a suboptimal #9 spot in the order rendered him too risky to start in a 5x5 format where efficiency is paramount. We are also monitoring the stagnant statuses of **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino** on the IL, whose absences continue to test the depth of our bench. As we look at the margins, **Zach McKinstry** (40.42) barely cleared the floor; his matchup against Burke is unfavorable, but his roster utility remains superior to the risk of playing a benched option against a pitcher as dominant as Cease. \n\nRisks today are concentrated on players facing high-caliber arms; **Austin Riley** (49.30) and **Isaac Paredes** (54.18) are facing pitchers in Soroka and Woo who depress their offensive ceilings. While **Austin Riley** is relegated to the bottom of the order, he remains a marginal start only because our depth\u2014specifically the inability to sub in **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Dalton Rushing**, or **Edwin Arroyo**\u2014forces our hand. We will keep a close eye on weather developments, as any significant shifts could plummet the scores of **Mickey Moniak** and the outfield core, potentially forcing a defensive lineup adjustment before the first pitch.",
